== CANON-2 (v3.34, decided by Marcelo Fortes): hexadecimal literals may be
== written `$FF` or `0xFF` (`0X` too), with the digit separator `_`. A leading
== zero never means octal: `017` is seventeen.
Module Runtime.HexLiterals

Const Mask := 0xFF_FF

Main :
    X := 0xff + 0X10
    PutLn(X)
    PutLn(Mask)
    PutLn(0xFF = $FF)
    PutLn(017)
;
